ay_food_intake\u003e\n\u003c/user_today_nutrition\u003e\n\n\u003cphysical_environment\u003e\ncurrent datetime: Thu, 26 Feb 2026 11:12:41 +0000\nUTC offset: Z\n\u003c/physical_environment\u003e\n\nYou have approximately 20 dishes to work with. Each dish has a unique `id` field — you MUST use this exact `id` as the `dish_id` in your output. Do not change, re-format, or fabricate any ID.\n\n\u003cfiltered_recipes\u003e\n[{\"ID\":8637,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":24795,\"FoodName\":\"Ground Sausage Spaghetti\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/8304855.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":558,\"ProteinG\":23.7,\"CarbsG\":62.6,\"FatG\":22.7,\"Ingredients\":[\"1 (16 ounce) package spaghetti\",\"1 pound ground sausage\",\"½ onion, chopped\",\"½ green bell pepper, chopped\",\"2 tablespoons margarine\",\"1 (14.5 ounce) can diced tomatoes\",\"1 (6 ounce) can tomato sauce\",\"½ teaspoon Italian seasoning\",\"¼ cup grated Parmesan cheese, or more to taste\",\"¼ cup shredded mozzarella cheese, or more to taste\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Bring a large pot of lightly salted water to a boil. Cook spaghetti in the boiling water, stirring occasionally, until cooked through but firm to the bite, about 12 minutes. Drain.\",\"Cook and stir sausage in a large skillet over medium-high heat until browned and crumbly, 5 to 7 minutes. Drain and discard grease. Stir onion, bell pepper, and margarine into sausage. Reduce heat to low, cover, and cook until onion is soft, 3 to 5 minutes.\",\"Stir tomatoes, tomato sauce, and Italian seasoning into sausage mixture; bring to a boil. Stir in Parmesan cheese and pour over cooked spaghetti. Top with mozzarella.\"]},{\"ID\":10692,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":25125,\"FoodName\":\"Catelli Bistro Kale Caesar Pasta Salad\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/3544275.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":472.1,\"ProteinG\":17.4,\"CarbsG\":55.3,\"FatG\":21.8,\"Ingredients\":[\"1 (375 g) package Catelli Bistro® Tri-Colour Fusilli\",\"6 cups thinly sliced kale\",\"8 slices bacon, cooked and crumbled\",\"⅓ cup mayonnaise\",\"3 tablespoons lemon juice\",\"2 tablespoons olive oil\",\"1 teaspoon garlic puree\",\"1 teaspoon Dijon mustard\",\"1 teaspoon anchovy paste\",\"½ teaspoon salt\",\"½ teaspoon freshly ground pepper\",\"2 tablespoons finely shredded Parmesan cheese\",\"1 Lemon wedges\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Cook pasta according to package directions. Drain and rinse under cold water; transfer to large bowl. Add kale and bacon; toss well.\",\"Whisk together mayonnaise, lemon juice, olive oil, garlic puree, mustard, anchovy paste, salt and pepper. Drizzle over pasta and toss to coat well. Sprinkle with Parmesan. Serve with lemon wedges.\"]},{\"ID\":14287,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":10789,\"FoodName\":\"Impossible Pumpkin Pie II\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/521801.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":228.4,\"ProteinG\":5.6,\"CarbsG\":31.5,\"FatG\":9.2,\"Ingredients\":[\"¾ cup white sugar\",\"½ cup biscuit baking mix\",\"2 tablespoons butter\",\"1 (12 fluid ounce) can evaporated milk\",\"2 eggs\",\"1 (15 ounce) can solid pack pumpkin puree\",\"2 ½ teaspoons pumpkin pie spice\",\"2 teaspoons vanilla extract\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Lightly grease a 9 inch pie pan.\",\"In a large bowl, combine sugar and baking mix. Stir in butter, milk and eggs. Then beat in pumpkin, spice and vanilla to mixture until smooth. Pour into pie pan.\",\"Bake in preheated oven for 50 to 55 minutes, or until knife inserted in center comes out clean. Refrigerate any remaining pie. High altitude directions: Bake at 375  degrees F (190 degrees C) for 45 to 50 minutes.\"]},{\"ID\":23189,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":5547,\"FoodName\":\"Tomatoes with Seafood Dressing\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/2002120.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":318.8,\"ProteinG\":12.4,\"CarbsG\":11.6,\"FatG\":25.5,\"Ingredients\":[\"1 cup canned shrimp\",\"2 hard-cooked eggs, chopped\",\"1 ½ cups finely grated carrots\",\"1 tablespoon minced onion\",\"½ teaspoon salt\",\"⅛ teaspoon ground black pepper\",\"½ cup mayonnaise\",\"2 tablespoons lemon juice\",\"½ teaspoon prepared mustard\",\"4 medium tomatoes\",\"4 leaves of lettuce\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Add shrimp, eggs, carrots, onion, salt, and pepper to the bowl of a food processor.  Pulse until just combined.  Blend mayonnaise with lemon juice and mustard; mix into shrimp mixture with a fork.\",\"Core tomatoes. Cut into quarters without cutting all the way to the bottom. Place each tomato on a lettuce leaf, and open.  Spoon shrimp mixture into the center.  Serve\"]},{\"ID\":24586,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":28525,\"FoodName\":\"Baked Bananas\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/4542583.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":168.3,\"ProteinG\":1.4,\"CarbsG\":42.4,\"FatG\":0.9,\"Ingredients\":[\"cooking spray\",\"4 firm bananas, peeled and halved lengthwise\",\"¼ cup maple syrup\",\"1 tablespoon ground cinnamon\",\"1 (1 inch) piece fresh ginger, grated\",\"1 ½ teaspoons ground nutmeg\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Preheat oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Spray a baking dish with cooking spray.\",\"Arrange banana halves in the prepared baking dish. Drizzle maple syrup over bananas and top with cinnamon, ginger, and nutmeg. Cover dish with aluminum foil.\",\"Bake in the preheated oven until heated through, 10 to 15 minutes.\"]},{\"ID\":30069,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":29393,\"FoodName\":\"Raspberry Fudge Truffles\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/6407242.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":95.9,\"ProteinG\":1,\"CarbsG\":11.8,\"FatG\":5.7,\"Ingredients\":[\"1 cup semisweet chocolate chips\",\"1 (8 ounce) package cream cheese, softened\",\"¾ cup crushed vanilla wafers\",\"½ cup seedless raspberry jam\",\"1 cup semisweet chocolate chips\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Microwave 1 cup chocolate chips in a microwave-safe bowl on low in 30-second intervals, stirring after each melting, until chocolate is smooth and warm, 1 to 3 minutes. Do not overheat or chocolate will scorch.\",\"Beat cream cheese into melted chocolate until smooth; stir in wafer crumbs and raspberry jam. Cover and refrigerate until mixture is semi-firm, about 4 hours.\",\"Roll chocolate-cream cheese mixture into 1-inch balls and place on a baking sheet or platter. Freeze until firm, about 1 hour.\",\"Melt remaining 1 cup chocolate chips in the microwave, 1 to 3 minutes, stirring every 30 seconds. Dip frozen chocolate balls into melted chocolate; allow chocolate to set before serving.\"]},{\"ID\":36960,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":17033,\"FoodName\":\"Arnold Palmer\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/747148.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":33.9,\"ProteinG\":0.1,\"CarbsG\":8.9,\"FatG\":0,\"Ingredients\":[\"⅓ cup iced tea\",\"⅓ cup prepared lemonade\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Pour the iced tea and lemonade into an ice-filled glass; stir to mix.\"]},{\"ID\":41990,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":33513,\"FoodName\":\"Godfather\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/8097073.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":181.3,\"ProteinG\":0,\"CarbsG\":14,\"FatG\":0.1,\"Ingredients\":[\"1 fluid ounce Scotch whiskey\",\"1 fluid ounce amaretto liqueur\"],\"Instructions\":[\"In a rocks glass with ice, combine the scotch and amaretto. Stir.\"]},{\"ID\":48668,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":35679,\"FoodName\":\"Alan's Ultimate Bran Muffins\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/778113.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":280.3,\"ProteinG\":10.1,\"CarbsG\":54.4,\"FatG\":7.2,\"Ingredients\":[\"1 cup whole wheat flour\",\"1 cup wheat germ\",\"2 ¾ cups wheat bran\",\"⅔ cup oat bran\",\"2 teaspoons baking powder\",\"2 teaspoons baking soda\",\"2 teaspoons ground ginger\",\"1 tablespoon barley malt flour\",\"3 tablespoons vegetable oil\",\"⅔ cup honey\",\"1 ¼ cups reduced-fat milk\",\"1 cup low-fat plain yogurt\",\"2 eggs, beaten\",\"1 cup raisins\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). Lightly grease a 12 cup muffin pan.\",\"In a medium bowl, mix whole wheat flour, wheat germ, wheat bran, oat bran, baking powder, baking soda, ground ginger, and barley malt flour.\",\"In a separate medium bowl, thoroughly blend oil, honey, milk, yogurt, and eggs. Gradually fold milk mixture into the whole wheat flour mixture until moistened. Fold in the raisins. Spoon into the prepared muffin pan.\",\"Bake 20 to 25 minutes in the preheated oven, or until a toothpick inserted in the center of a muffin comes out clean.\"]},{\"ID\":59681,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":22639,\"FoodName\":\"Memphis Style Back Ribs\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/2354819.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":2659.5,\"ProteinG\":147.8,\"CarbsG\":21.1,\"FatG\":215.7,\"Ingredients\":[\"¼ cup brown sugar\",\"¼ cup kosher salt\",\"2 teaspoons chili powder\",\"1 ½ teaspoons dry mustard\",\"1 teaspoon black pepper\",\"1 teaspoon celery salt\",\"2 racks Smithfield® Extra Tender Pork Back Ribs, membrane removed\",\"¼ cup prepared yellow mustard\",\"Apple juice, in a spray bottle\"],\"Instructions\":[\"About 30 minutes before smoking, make the dry rub.  Combine all ingredients in a small bowl; mix well.\",\"Spread both sides of ribs with yellow mustard and sprinkle with dry rub. Let stand at room temperature for 30 minutes.\",\"Heat charcoal or gas grill for indirect cooking at 250 degrees F.  Place the ribs, meaty side up, over a drip pan and cook for 4 to 6 hours until very tender. Spritz ribs occasionally with water or apple juice using a spray bottle.  Add about 12 coals to a charcoal grill every 45 minutes or so to maintain the heat.\",\"Let ribs stand 10 to 15 minutes before serving.\"]},{\"ID\":70394,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":95287,\"FoodName\":\"Caramel Apple Bars I\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/909847.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":141.5,\"ProteinG\":1.5,\"CarbsG\":21.6,\"FatG\":5.9,\"Ingredients\":[\"2 cups all-purpose flour\",\"2 cups quick cooking oats\",\"1 ½ cups packed brown sugar\",\"1 teaspoon baking soda\",\"1 ¼ cups butter\",\"1 ½ cups caramel ice cream topping\",\"½ cup all-purpose flour\",\"2 cups chopped apples\",\"½ cup chopped walnuts\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F.  Grease a 15 x 10 x 1 inch pan.\",\"In a small pan over low heat, melt the butter or margarine.  In large bowl, combine 2 cups flour, 2 cups quick cooking oats, brown sugar, baking soda, and melted butter or margarine.  Mix until crumbly.  Press half of mixture (about 2-1/2 cups) in the greased pan. Set aside the rest.  Bake for 8 minutes.\",\"In a small pan over medium heat, combine caramel topping and 1/2 cup flour. Bring to a boil, stirring constantly. Still stirring constantly, boil for 2 or 3 minutes until slightly thickened.  Spread apples and nuts onto the baked crust.  Pour hot caramel mixture evenly over apples and nuts. Sprinkle reserved crumbly mixture evenly over the top.\",\"Return pan to oven.  Bake 20-25 minutes or until golden brown. Cool completely in pan.  Cut into bars. (Refrigeration makes cutting easier). Store tightly covered.\"]},{\"ID\":83846,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":85082,\"FoodName\":\"Healthy Vegetarian Quiche\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/1940589.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":410.5,\"ProteinG\":12.6,\"CarbsG\":40.5,\"FatG\":22.5,\"Ingredients\":[\"1 tablespoon oil, or as desired\",\"1 small onion, chopped\",\"5 cups mixed vegetables\",\"2 tablespoons lemon juice\",\"1 pinch salt\",\"4 large eggs\",\"¾ cup crumbled feta cheese\",\"½ cup milk\",\"¼ cup shredded mozzarella cheese\",\"salt and ground black pepper to taste\",\"½ cup cold water\",\"½ cup corn oil\",\"2 ½ cups all-purpose flour\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Preheat oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C).\",\"Heat oil in a skillet over medium heat; cook and stir onion until golden brown, 10 to 15 minutes. Add vegetables, lemon juice, and 1 pinch salt to onion; stir well. Remove skillet from heat.\",\"Mix eggs, feta cheese, milk, mozzarella cheese, salt, and pepper together in a separate bowl.\",\"Mix cold water and corn oil together in a bowl. Place flour and 1 pinch salt in a separate bowl. Slowly pour oil mixture into flour mixture, mixing until a thick dough forms. Press the dough into two 9-inch round baking pans. Spoon the vegetable mixture into the crusts and top with egg mixture.\",\"Bake in the preheated oven until quiches are set in the middle, about 20 minutes.\"]},{\"ID\":104117,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":90961,\"FoodName\":\"Instant Pot\\u0026reg; Protein-Packed Vegetarian Chili\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/7349506.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":225.4,\"ProteinG\":19.1,\"CarbsG\":26,\"FatG\":6.1,\"Ingredients\":[\"2 teaspoons olive oil\",\"1 cup chopped onion\",\"½ cup chopped green bell pepper\",\"½ cup chopped red bell pepper\",\"2 cloves garlic, minced\",\"1 pound vegetarian ground beef substitute (such as Beyond Meat® Beyond Beef®)\",\"1 (15 ounce) can chili beans\",\"1 (14.5 ounce) can diced tomatoes\",\"2 tablespoons chili powder\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Turn on a multi-functional pressure cooker (such as Instant Pot\\u0026reg;) and select Saute function. Add oil, onion, and bell peppers. Saute until tender, about 3 minutes. Add garlic and cook until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Add ground beef substitute. Stir, breaking up into crumbles. Add beans, tomatoes, and chili powder. Hit Cancel.\",\"Close and lock the lid. Select high pressure according to manufacturer's instructions; set timer for 5 minutes. Allow 10 to 15 minutes for pressure to build.\",\"Release pressure carefully using the quick-release method according to manufacturer's instructions, about 5 minutes. Unlock and remove the lid. Serve immediately.\"]},{\"ID\":119918,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":134819,\"FoodName\":\"Feijoada Nordestino (Northeastern Brazilian Black Bean Stew)\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/1315131.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":466.9,\"ProteinG\":12.2,\"CarbsG\":77,\"FatG\":12.1,\"Ingredients\":[\"½ (15 ounce) can black beans, rinsed and drained\",\"1 onion, diced\",\"¼ pound smoked ham, diced\",\"¼ pound calabresa (Portuguese smoked sausage), cut into 1/4-inch slices\",\"4 cloves garlic, minced, divided\",\"1 ½ teaspoons salt\",\"1 tablespoon ground cumin\",\"½ teaspoon ground black pepper\",\"1 bay leaf\",\"1 ½ teaspoons olive oil\",\"4 leaves collard greens, cut into fine ribbons, or to taste\",\"1 ½ cups cassava flour\",\"1 ½ teaspoons butter, or to taste\",\"4 cups cooked white rice\",\"4 oranges, cut in wedges, or as desired\",\"¼ cup coarsely chopped cilantro\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Combine beans, onion, ham, calabresa, 3 cloves garlic, salt, cumin, black pepper, and bay leaf in a pressure cooker; cover with water to fill line.\",\"Close cooker securely and place pressure regulator over vent according to manufacturer's instructions. Cook at high pressure until regulator is gently rocking, 5 to 7 minutes. Reduce pressure to low. Cook, adding water halfway if needed, until beans are tender and water is reduced to your liking, about 1 hour.\",\"Turn off heat. Let pressure release naturally according to manufacturer's instructions, about 5 minutes. Unlock lid and remove. Let feijoada cool until ready to serve.\",\"Heat olive oil in a saucepan over medium-high heat. Saute remaining 1 clove garlic and collard greens until just tender, about 2 minutes.\",\"Place cassava flour in a skillet over medium-high heat. Cook and stir until toasted, about 3 minutes. Stir in butter.\",\"Serve feijoada with the collards-garlic mixture, toasted cassava flour, rice, orange wedges, and cilantro.\"]},{\"ID\":124902,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":116150,\"FoodName\":\"Chilled Strawberry Soup\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/4500846.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":252,\"ProteinG\":4.3,\"CarbsG\":14.4,\"FatG\":20.4,\"Ingredients\":[\"2 cups \\u003ca href=\\\"https://www.allrecipes.com/article/how-to-freeze-strawberries/\\\" aria-label=\\\"frozen strawberries\\\"\\u003efrozen strawberries\\u003c/a\\u003e\",\"2 cups milk\",\"1 cup heavy cream\",\"½ cup sour cream\",\"2 tablespoons white sugar, or to taste\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Puree strawberries, milk, cream and sour cream in a blender or food processor until smooth.  Stir in sugar to taste.  Chill 8 hours or overnight in refrigerator before serving.\"]},{\"ID\":140711,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":125517,\"FoodName\":\"Spicy Mango-Basil Paletas\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/1323597.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":82.1,\"ProteinG\":0.4,\"CarbsG\":21.7,\"FatG\":0.2,\"Ingredients\":[\"3 mangos - peeled, seeded, and cut into chunks\",\"1 tablespoon chopped fresh basil\",\"2 limes, juiced\",\"½ teaspoon cayenne pepper\",\"¼ teaspoon salt\",\"½ cup white sugar\",\"1 mango, peeled, seeded, and diced\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Blend mango chunks, basil, lime juice, cayenne pepper, and salt in a blender until smooth; pour into a large bowl. Stir sugar into mango mixture until sugar dissolves. Fold diced mango into mixture. Pour into freezer pop molds.\",\"Freeze until firm, 14 to 24 hours.\"]},{\"ID\":141802,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":143179,\"FoodName\":\"Almond Flour Brownies\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/2229073.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":215,\"ProteinG\":3.3,\"CarbsG\":24.3,\"FatG\":13.5,\"Ingredients\":[\"¾ cup blanched almond flour\",\"⅔ cup agave nectar\",\"½ cup chopped walnuts\",\"2 eggs\",\"5 tablespoons unsweetened cocoa powder\",\"¼ cup coconut oil\",\"1 teaspoon vanilla extract\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).\",\"Mix almond flour, agave nectar, walnuts, eggs, cocoa powder, coconut oil, and vanilla extract together in a bowl; spread into an 8-inch square baking dish.\",\"Bake in the preheated oven until edges of brownies begin to pull from sides of dish, about 30 minutes. Let brownies cool slightly before slicing, about 5 minutes.\"]},{\"ID\":146461,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":130477,\"FoodName\":\"Tammy's Fish Chowder\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/1963937.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":354.4,\"ProteinG\":9.5,\"CarbsG\":31.9,\"FatG\":19.9,\"Ingredients\":[\"1 tablespoon olive oil\",\"1 tablespoon butter\",\"2 yellow onions, diced\",\"3 ribs celery, diced\",\"½ cup white wine\",\"4 potatoes, chopped\",\"2 cups fish stock\",\"1 tablespoon chopped fresh thyme\",\"1 teaspoon seafood seasoning (such as Old Bay®)\",\"1 bay leaf\",\"salt and ground black pepper to taste\",\"1 cup heavy whipping cream\",\"1 (4 ounce) fillet sea bass, chopped, or more to taste\",\"½ teaspoon white sugar\",\"3 dashes hot sauce\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Heat olive oil and butter in a large stockpot over medium heat; cook and stir onions and celery in the hot oil until softened, about 5 minutes. Add wine; raise heat to medium-high and cook until wine is reduced by half, 2 to 3 minutes.\",\"Mix potatoes, fish stock, thyme, seafood seasoning, bay leaf, salt, and pepper into onion mixture; bring to a boil, reduce heat to medium-low, cover stockpot, and simmer until potatoes are tender but not falling apart, 10 to 15 minutes.\",\"Heat cream in a small saucepan over medium heat just until cream is steaming, about 5 minutes. Stir cream and sea bass into potato mixture; cook until sea bass is cooked through, about 10 minutes. Season chowder with sugar, hot sauce, salt, and pepper.\"]}]\n\u003c/filtered_recipes\u003e"},{"text":"Event: lunch_1100"}],"role":"user"}},{"role":"model","meta":{"run_id":"2026022611124101KJCTD9Q5AXP6MRH1Z0C73Q1J","entrance":"lunch_1100","history_version":1,"event_type":"lunch_1100"},"custom_content":{"items":[{"text":"**Defining the Problem**\n\nI'm focused on Codes's needs and the challenges she faces. I've pinpointed the \"8 PM dessert monster\" as the main hurdle to her fat loss goal. Considering it's lunchtime, I'm already formulating strategies to address the late-night hunger, focusing on the available information.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Lunch Strategy**\n\nNow I'm diving deeper into lunch options for Codes, aiming for high protein and satiety to combat the evening cravings. Considering her low current intake, I'm leaning toward higher calorie choices like ground sausage spaghetti, or the instant pot chili. I need to make sure the chosen meals are unique.\n\n\n**Refining the Choices**\n\nI'm now carefully curating the lunch options, focusing on high protein and satiety as planned. The chili and muffins is solid, and I've locked in the ground sausage spaghetti. Considering the existing calorie targets, I am rethinking the third option, aiming for something lower in calories to offer more flexibility for the rest of the day. The Tomatoes with Seafood Dressing and the Pasta salad are too high for this round.\n\n\n**Finalizing Lunch Solutions**\n\nI've decided on three distinct lunch recipes for Codes. First, the \"High-Protein Chili \u0026 Bran Power Pair,\" and second, the \"Savory Sausage Spaghetti Reset.\" The third option is the \"Kale Caesar \u0026 Bacon Pasta Salad\". I'm aiming for varied choices with good protein and calorie balance to keep her satisfied through the afternoon, and will also suggest three additional non-active recipes to give more choices.\n\n\n**Analyzing Recipe Recommendations**\n\nI'm now satisfied with the final recipe list for Codes, incorporating both active and non-active choices with good protein and calorie balance. I've double-checked dish repetition and recipe IDs. I'm also crafting supportive and engaging descriptions for each recipe.\n\n\n**Evaluating the Recipes**\n\nI am now thoroughly reviewing each recipe, confirming the calorie and protein counts, and verifying that the dish ID's are correct. Furthermore, I've checked the recipe text, and made certain each recipe description uses a smart, sassy, supportive tone, for the best effect on Codes!\n\n\n"},{"text":"{\n  \"recipes\": [\n    {\n      \"recipe_title\": \"High-Protein Chili \u0026 Bran Power Pair\",\n      \"recipe_subtitle\": \"#InsulinStabilizer #HighFiber #HungerProof\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"Since yesterday was a bit quiet on the logs, this fiber-and-protein duo is your ultimate metabolic reset. It stabilizes your blood sugar now so the 8 PM dessert monster doesn't even stand a chance tonight. Deal?\",\n      \"dishes\": [\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"104117\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Main Dish\",\n            \"High Protein\",\n            \"Stable Energy\",\n            \"One-Pot\",\n            \"Vegetarian\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"48668\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Side Dish\",\n            \"High Fiber\",\n            \"Low Sugar\",\n            \"Stable Energy\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"recipe_title\": \"Savory Sausage Spaghetti Reset\",\n      \"recipe_subtitle\": \"#ComfortFood #SatietyScore #HomeCooking\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"Going for a savory, substantial lunch at home is a systems-level win for your fat loss journey. This keeps you physically full and mentally satisfied, making those late-night sugar cravings feel much less 'loud' later on.\",\n      \"dishes\": [\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"8637\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Complete Meal\",\n            \"Savory\",\n            \"High Protein\",\n            \"Comfort Food\",\n            \"Medium Effort\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"recipe_title\": \"Kale Caesar \u0026 Bacon Pasta Salad\",\n      \"recipe_subtitle\": \"#StableEnergy #HighProtein #SavoryKick\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"This is the 'clean energy' trifecta: protein, healthy fats, and greens. It’s light enough to keep you moving but has the bacon and parmesan kick to satisfy your brain's reward center without a sugar crash.\",\n      \"dishes\": [\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"10692\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Complete Meal\",\n            \"High Protein\",\n            \"Stable Energy\",\n            \"Savory\",\n            \"Low Effort\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"recipe_title\": \"Northeastern Brazilian Black Bean Stew\",\n      \"recipe_subtitle\": \"#SlowCarbs #HighSatiety #ComfortFood\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"If you're feeling like you need a warm hug in a bowl, this black bean stew is it. The slow-digesting carbs and protein from the ham and sausage provide a steady release of energy that protects your willpower for the evening.\",\n      \"dishes\": [\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"119918\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Complete Meal\",\n            \"Savory\",\n            \"Comfort Food\",\n            \"Stable Energy\",\n            \"High Satiety\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"recipe_title\": \"Healthy Veggie \u0026 Feta Quiche\",\n      \"recipe_subtitle\": \"#VeggiePacked #SatietyScore #ProteinAnchor\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"A veggie-heavy lunch is a great way to load up on volume without the calorie bloat. The eggs and feta provide the protein anchor you need to keep your insulin levels from spiking and crashing before dinner.\",\n      \"dishes\": [\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"83846\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Main Dish\",\n            \"Vegetarian\",\n            \"High Volume\",\n            \"Protein Score\",\n            \"Savory\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"recipe_title\": \"Seafood-Stuffed Tomato Plate\",\n      \"recipe_subtitle\": \"#LightLunch #HighProtein #LowCarb\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"When you want something fresh but need to keep your protein goals on track, this is your play. It’s high in satiety thanks to the shrimp and eggs, keeping you fueled without feeling heavy.\",\n      \"dishes\": [\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"23189\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Complete Meal\",\n            \"High Protein\",\n            \"Low Carb\",\n            \"Fresh\",\n            \"Low Effort\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"role":"model"}},{"role":"user","meta":{"run_id":"2026022611124101KJCTD9Q5AXP6MRH1Z0C73Q1J","entrance":"lunch_1100","history_version":1,"event_type":"lunch_1100"},"custom_content":{"items":[{"text":"\