bowl, and whisk the cornstarch mixture into the hot gravy. Allow the gravy to simmer until thickened, about 3 minutes. Stir in salt to taste; strain out any large pieces of rosemary before serving.\"]},{\"ID\":31615,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":47428,\"FoodName\":\"Turkey Mushroom Gravy\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/3387491.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":347.2,\"ProteinG\":3,\"CarbsG\":9.1,\"FatG\":34,\"Ingredients\":[\"2 cups unsalted butter\",\"1 pound portobello mushrooms, wiped clean with paper towels\",\"2 pounds whole white mushrooms, wiped clean with paper towels\",\"1 cup all-purpose flour\",\"4 (14.5 ounce) cans chicken broth\",\"1 ½ cups turkey pan drippings\",\"2 cups chopped onions\",\"1 cup chopped celery\",\"salt and pepper to taste\",\"¼ teaspoon cayenne pepper\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Melt butter in a large stock pot over medium-low heat, and cook the mushrooms until they are browned and the butter is clear, 1 to 1 1/2 hours. Remove the mushrooms, coarsely chop them, and set aside. There should be about 1 cup of butter left in the stock pot; whisk the flour into the butter, and gently cook over low heat until the flour mixture turns mahogany brown in color, about 20 minutes. Whisk in the chicken broth; bring the mixture to a simmer to thicken the stock.\",\"Pour the turkey drippings into a saucepan, then cook and stir the onions and celery in the drippings over medium-low heat until the onions begin to turn brown, about 20 minutes. Stir the drippings and vegetables into the thickened stock. Bring the gravy to a gentle boil, reduce heat, and simmer for about 20 minutes to blend the flavors. Stir in the chopped mushrooms, then season to taste with salt, black pepper, and cayenne pepper.\"]},{\"ID\":54765,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":58103,\"FoodName\":\"Fried Calamari\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/8887907.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":523.2,\"ProteinG\":22.9,\"CarbsG\":79.8,\"FatG\":11.6,\"Ingredients\":[\"1 pound calamari tubes, thawed if frozen\",\"peanut oil for frying\",\"6 cups all-purpose flour\",\"2 cups whole milk\",\"4 eggs\",\"1 tablespoon cornstarch\",\"1 tablespoon paprika\",\"1 teaspoon salt\",\"1 teaspoon finely ground black pepper \",\"½ teaspoon cayenne pepper\",\"1 tablespoon fresh parsley, or to taste\",\"1 wedge lemon\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Check calamari for breaks and slice into 1/8- to 1/4-inch rings.\",\"Heat oil in a deep-fryer or large saucepan to 400 degrees F (200 degrees C).\",\"Place 2 cups flour in a bowl. Whisk milk and eggs together in a separate bowl. Place remaining 4 cups flour, cornstarch, paprika, salt, pepper, and cayenne in a third bowl; mix thoroughly.\",\"Toss calamari rings in the plain flour. Move to the egg mixture and thoroughly coat. Move to the seasoned flour and coat fully. Move back to egg mixture if not thoroughly coated; coat with seasoned flour again.\",\"Submerge floured calamari in the hot oil until golden, 3 to 4 minutes per batch. Lift out with a slotted spoon, letting oil drip off. Drain on paper towels. Place calamari in a small bowl; check seasoning. Add parsley and lemon wedge for garnish.\"]},{\"ID\":54766,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":58104,\"FoodName\":\"Fried Calamari\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/8887907.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":523.2,\"ProteinG\":22.9,\"CarbsG\":79.8,\"FatG\":11.6,\"Ingredients\":[\"1 pound calamari tubes, thawed if frozen\",\"peanut oil for frying\",\"6 cups all-purpose flour\",\"2 cups whole milk\",\"4 eggs\",\"1 tablespoon cornstarch\",\"1 tablespoon paprika\",\"1 teaspoon salt\",\"1 teaspoon finely ground black pepper \",\"½ teaspoon cayenne pepper\",\"1 tablespoon fresh parsley, or to taste\",\"1 wedge lemon\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Check calamari for breaks and slice into 1/8- to 1/4-inch rings.\",\"Heat oil in a deep-fryer or large saucepan to 400 degrees F (200 degrees C).\",\"Place 2 cups flour in a bowl. Whisk milk and eggs together in a separate bowl. Place remaining 4 cups flour, cornstarch, paprika, salt, pepper, and cayenne in a third bowl; mix thoroughly.\",\"Toss calamari rings in the plain flour. Move to the egg mixture and thoroughly coat. Move to the seasoned flour and coat fully. Move back to egg mixture if not thoroughly coated; coat with seasoned flour again.\",\"Submerge floured calamari in the hot oil until golden, 3 to 4 minutes per batch. Lift out with a slotted spoon, letting oil drip off. Drain on paper towels. Place calamari in a small bowl; check seasoning. Add parsley and lemon wedge for garnish.\"]},{\"ID\":74171,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":82766,\"FoodName\":\"Amazing Italian Lemon Butter Chicken\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/223009.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":659.6,\"ProteinG\":26.8,\"CarbsG\":37.4,\"FatG\":44.9,\"Ingredients\":[\"¼ cup white wine\",\"5 tablespoons fresh lemon juice\",\"5 tablespoons heavy cream\",\"1 cup butter, chilled\",\"salt and pepper to taste\",\"½ pound dry farfalle (bow tie) pasta\",\"4 skinless, boneless chicken breast halves - pounded to 1/4 inch thickness\",\"1 tablespoon olive oil\",\"1 tablespoon butter\",\"¼ cup all-purpose flour\",\"salt and pepper to taste\",\"4 ounces bacon\",\"6 ounces mushrooms, sliced\",\"6 ounces artichoke hearts, drained and halved\",\"2 teaspoons capers, drained\",\"chopped fresh parsley for garnish\"],\"Instructions\":[\"To make the sauce, pour the wine and lemon juice into a saucepan over medium heat. Cook at a low boil until the liquid is reduced by 1/3. Stir in cream, and simmer until it thickens. Gradually add the butter 1 tablespoon at a time to the sauce, stirring until completely incorporated. Season with salt and pepper. Remove from heat, and keep warm.\",\"Bring a large pot of lightly salted water to boil. Add pasta, and cook until al dente, about 8 to 10 minutes. Drain, and set aside.\",\"To make the chicken, heat oil and 2 tablespoons butter in a large skillet over medium heat. In a bowl, stir together flour, salt, and pepper. Lightly coat chicken with flour mixture. Without crowding, carefully place chicken in hot oil. (If necessary, cook in batches.) Fry until cooked through and golden brown on both sides. Remove the chicken to paper towels. Stir the bacon, mushrooms, artichokes, and capers into the oil; cook until the mushrooms are soft.\",\"Cut the chicken breasts into bite-size strips, and return them to the skillet. Stir half of the lemon butter sauce into the chicken mixture.\",\"To serve, place pasta in a large bowl. Stir the chicken mixture into the pasta. Taste, and adjust seasonings. Stir in additional lemon butter sauce as desired. Toss well, and garnish with parsley.\"]},{\"ID\":74173,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":82768,\"FoodName\":\"Lemony Garlic Shrimp with Pasta\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/872692.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":502.2,\"ProteinG\":33.4,\"CarbsG\":44.9,\"FatG\":20.1,\"Ingredients\":[\"¾ cup kosher salt\",\"1 gallon cold water\",\"2 pounds peeled and deveined large shrimp (21 to 30 per pound)\",\"1 (16 ounce) package angel hair pasta\",\"¼ cup unsalted butter\",\"¼ cup olive oil\",\"3 tablespoons minced garlic\",\"⅓ cup white wine\",\"¼ cup lemon juice\",\"½ teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes\",\"1 teaspoon freshly ground black pepper\",\"½ cup chopped fresh parsley\",\"1 tablespoon lemon zest\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Dissolve the kosher salt in 1 gallon of water in a large pot. Add the shrimp, and refrigerate 2 to 4 hours. Drain and pat shrimp dry with paper towels.\",\"Fill a large pot with lightly salted water and bring to a rolling boil over high heat. Once the water is boiling, stir in the angel hair pasta, and return to a boil. Cook the pasta uncovered, stirring occasionally, until the pasta has cooked through but is still firm to the bite, 4 to 5 minutes. Drain well in a colander set in the sink.\",\"Meanwhile, melt the butter and olive oil in a large skillet over medium-low heat. Stir in the garlic, and cook until softened, 3 to 4 minutes. Add the shrimp, white wine, lemon juice, and red pepper flakes. Cook and stir until the shrimp is no longer translucent in the center, about 6 minutes. Stir in the black pepper, parsley, and lemon zest before tossing with the angel hair pasta.\"]},{\"ID\":76066,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":71347,\"FoodName\":\"Old Fashioned Brown Gravy\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/324242.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":60.5,\"ProteinG\":5.4,\"CarbsG\":5.8,\"FatG\":1.6,\"Ingredients\":[\"2 tablespoons pan drippings\",\"2 tablespoons all-purpose flour\",\"1 cup milk\",\"1 cup water\",\"salt and pepper to taste\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Immediately after removing meat from a roasting pan or other pan, drain off the drippings, reserving 2 tablespoons. Sprinkle the flour over drippings; cook and stir over medium heat until brown. Gradually stir in milk, whisking with a fork to scrape up all of the meaty bits from the pan, then gradually whisk in the water. Increase the heat to medium-high, and cook, stirring constantly, until the gravy thickens, about 10 minutes. Taste, and season with salt and pepper.\"]},{\"ID\":76069,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":71349,\"FoodName\":\"Healing Cabbage Soup\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://static.onecms.io/wp-content/uploads/sites/43/2019/12/3016182_healing-cabbage-soup_photo-by-julieruble.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":82.1,\"ProteinG\":1.5,\"CarbsG\":8.6,\"FatG\":5.2,\"Ingredients\":[\"3 tablespoons olive oil\",\"½ onion, chopped\",\"2 cloves garlic, chopped\",\"2 quarts water\",\"4 teaspoons chicken bouillon granules\",\"1 teaspoon salt, or to taste\",\"½ teaspoon black pepper, or to taste\",\"½ head cabbage, cored and coarsely chopped\",\"1 (14.5 ounce) can Italian-style stewed tomatoes, drained and diced\"],\"Instructions\":[\"In a large stockpot, heat olive oil over medium heat. Stir in onion and garlic; cook until onion is transparent, about 5 minutes.\",\"Stir in water, bouillon, salt, and pepper. Bring to a boil, then stir in cabbage. Simmer until cabbage wilts, about 10 minutes.\",\"Stir in tomatoes. Return to a boil, then simmer 15 to 30 minutes, stirring often.\"]},{\"ID\":92624,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":87061,\"FoodName\":\"Kale Soup Plus\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/2980104.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":367,\"ProteinG\":11.9,\"CarbsG\":59,\"FatG\":10.6,\"Ingredients\":[\"2 tablespoons olive oil\",\"1 onion, chopped\",\"1 tablespoon roasted garlic\",\"6 small potatoes (such as Klondike Gourmet® red skin potatoes), cut into bite-size pieces, or more to taste\",\"1 bunch kale, stems removed and discarded, leaves torn into bite-size pieces\",\"2 tablespoons sesame oil\",\"1 (14 ounce) can black beans, drained and rinsed\",\"4 drained oil-packed sun-dried tomatoes\",\"1 (32 ounce) carton chicken broth\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat; cook and stir onion and garlic in hot oil until onion is softened, 5 to 10 minutes. Stir potatoes into onion mixture and cook until potatoes are lightly browned, 2 to 3 minutes.\",\"Stir kale into potato mixture and drizzle in sesame oil. Cook and stir until kale is wilted, about 2 minutes. Stir black beans and sun-dried tomatoes into kale-potato mixture; pour in chicken broth. Simmer soup until potatoes are tender, about 30 minutes.\"]},{\"ID\":92625,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":87062,\"FoodName\":\"Kale Soup Plus\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/2980104.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":367,\"ProteinG\":11.9,\"CarbsG\":59,\"FatG\":10.6,\"Ingredients\":[\"2 tablespoons olive oil\",\"1 onion, chopped\",\"1 tablespoon roasted garlic\",\"6 small potatoes (such as Klondike Gourmet® red skin potatoes), cut into bite-size pieces, or more to taste\",\"1 bunch kale, stems removed and discarded, leaves torn into bite-size pieces\",\"2 tablespoons sesame oil\",\"1 (14 ounce) can black beans, drained and rinsed\",\"4 drained oil-packed sun-dried tomatoes\",\"1 (32 ounce) carton chicken broth\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Heat olive oil in a skillet over medium heat; cook and stir onion and garlic in hot oil until onion is softened, 5 to 10 minutes. Stir potatoes into onion mixture and cook until potatoes are lightly browned, 2 to 3 minutes.\",\"Stir kale into potato mixture and drizzle in sesame oil. Cook and stir until kale is wilted, about 2 minutes. Stir black beans and sun-dried tomatoes into kale-potato mixture; pour in chicken broth. Simmer soup until potatoes are tender, about 30 minutes.\"]},{\"ID\":93430,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":105811,\"FoodName\":\"Creamy Baked Asiago Chicken Breasts\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/6873758.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":322.2,\"ProteinG\":30.4,\"CarbsG\":5.7,\"FatG\":17.9,\"Ingredients\":[\"4 boneless, skinless chicken breasts\",\"½ cup grated Asiago cheese\",\"½ cup light mayonnaise\",\"¼ cup low-fat plain Greek yogurt\",\"¼ cup dry white wine\",\"1 ½ teaspoons dried oregano\",\"1 teaspoon garlic powder\",\"1 teaspoon onion powder\",\"1 pinch ground nutmeg\",\"freshly ground black pepper to taste\",\"1 tablespoon aged balsamic vinegar, or to taste\",\"2 tablespoons grated Asiago cheese, or to taste\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F (190 degrees C). Grease a 9x13-inch baking dish.\",\"Place chicken breasts in the prepared baking dish. Whisk together Asiago cheese, mayonnaise, Greek yogurt, wine, oregano, garlic powder, onion powder, and nutmeg in a small bowl. Pour evenly over chicken breasts.\",\"Bake, uncovered, in the preheated oven until chicken is no longer pink in the center and the juices run clear, 40 to 50 minutes. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read at least 165 degrees F (74 degrees C). Top with black pepper, balsamic vinegar, and additional Asiago cheese just before serving.\"]},{\"ID\":93431,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":105812,\"FoodName\":\"Fruity Chicken Salad with Tarragon\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/6973686.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":322.6,\"ProteinG\":16.4,\"CarbsG\":11.7,\"FatG\":24.3,\"Ingredients\":[\"1 ½ cups grilled skinless, boneless chicken thighs, chopped\",\"½ red apple - peeled, cored, and diced\",\"½ cup halved green grapes\",\"⅓ cup toasted chopped pecans\",\"¼ cup diced red onion\",\"¼ cup diced celery\",\"¼ cup mayonnaise\",\"¼ cup low-fat plain Greek yogurt\",\"2 tablespoons chopped fresh tarragon\",\"1 teaspoon Dijon mustard\",\"1 lime, zested and juiced\",\"salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Combine chicken, apple, grapes, pecans, red onion, and celery in a medium bowl.\",\"Whisk mayonnaise, yogurt, tarragon, Dijon mustard, and lime zest and juice together in a small bowl. Stir dressing into the chicken mixture. Season with salt and pepper.\"]},{\"ID\":104682,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":91143,\"FoodName\":\"Cranberry Curd\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/7423902.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":56.4,\"ProteinG\":0.6,\"CarbsG\":8.9,\"FatG\":2.3,\"Ingredients\":[\"1 (12 ounce) bag fresh cranberries\",\"¾ cup water\",\"½ cup white sugar\",\"3  large egg yolks egg yolks\",\"2 tablespoons butter\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Place cranberries in a medium saucepan. Add water and sugar and bring to a boil over medium heat. Reduce heat to medium-low and cook, stirring occasionally, until cranberries have burst, 8 to 10 minutes.\",\"Pour cranberry mixture into a food processor or blender; blend until smooth, 10 to 20 seconds. Reserve 1/3 cup and return remaining cranberry mixture to the saucepan over low heat.\",\"Whisk egg yolks together in a small bowl. Slowly add reserved cranberry mixture, whisking constantly. Slowly whisk egg-cranberry mixture back into the saucepan and continue whisking until thickened and the curd coats the back of a metal spoon, about 5 minutes. Add butter, 1 tablespoon at a time, whisking until melted and fully incorporated.\",\"Pour into a sterile jar and allow to cool. Curd keeps in the refrigerator for up to 1 week.\"]},{\"ID\":104683,\"CreatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"UpdatedAt\":\"2026-02-04T21:10:30Z\",\"DeletedAt\":null,\"RecipeID\":108961,\"FoodName\":\"Chinese Steamed Buns\",\"FoodImage\":\"https://images.media-allrecipes.com/userphotos/1121464.jpg\",\"EnergyKcal\":44.4,\"ProteinG\":1.1,\"CarbsG\":8.4,\"FatG\":0.7,\"Ingredients\":[\"1 tablespoon active dry yeast\",\"1 teaspoon white sugar\",\"¼ cup all-purpose flour\",\"¼ cup water\",\"½ cup warm water\",\"1 ½ cups all-purpose flour\",\"¼ teaspoon salt\",\"2 tablespoons white sugar\",\"1 tablespoon vegetable oil\",\"½ teaspoon baking powder\"],\"Instructions\":[\"Mix together yeast, 1 teaspoon sugar, 1/4 cup flour, and 1/4 cup warm water.  Allow to stand for 30 minutes.\",\"Mix in 1/2 cup warm water, flour, salt, 2 tablespoons sugar, and vegetable oil.  Knead until dough surface is smooth and elastic.  Roll over in a greased bowl, and let stand until triple in size, about 2 1/2 to 3 hours.\",\"Punch down dough, and spread out on a floured board.  Sprinkle baking powder evenly on surface, and knead for 5 minutes.  Divide dough into 2 parts, and place the piece you are not working with in a covered bowl.  Divide each half into 12 parts. Shape each part into a ball with smooth surface up. Put each ball on a wax paper square.   Let stand covered until double, about 30 minutes.\",\"Bring water to a boil in wok, and reduce heat to medium; the water should still be boiling.  Place steam-plate on a small wire rack in the middle of the wok. Transfer as many buns on wax paper as will comfortably fit onto steam-plate leaving 1 to 2 inches between the buns.  At least 2 inches space should be left between steam-plate and the wok.  Cover wok with lid.  Steam buns over boiling water for 15 minutes.\",\"REMOVE LID BEFORE you turn off heat, or else water will drip back onto bun surface and produce yellowish \\\"blisters\\\" on bun surfaces. Continue steaming batches of buns until all are cooked.\"]}]\n\u003c/filtered_recipes\u003e"},{"text":"Event: morning_0600"}],"role":"user"}},{"role":"model","meta":{"event_type":"morning_0600","run_id":"2026022506082401KJ9PKDCEPEVV4ARJ3AAJ5JWJ","entrance":"morning_0600","history_version":1},"custom_content":{"items":[{"text":"**Mapping Out Strategies**\n\nRight now, I'm at the 6 AM breakfast planning stage, focusing on how to fit the day's targets. Considering the user's sweet tooth, I need to design a meal plan that helps with the late-night hunger obstacle. I'm focusing on hitting the protein target while staying within the 1294-1694 kcal range.\n\n\n**Structuring Meal Options**\n\nNow, I'm digging into individual dishes, cross-referencing them against the user's needs. I've pinpointed a few promising options for breakfast that balance protein, sweetness, and practicality. The Fruity Chicken Salad and Creamy Baked Chicken Breasts are looking strong, alongside Cranberry Curd as a potential \"treat\" to combat cravings. I'm also assessing how the soups fit into the fiber/volume targets.\n\n\n**Comparing Breakfast Combinations**\n\nNow I'm actively comparing different breakfast combos. I've broken down each option: balancing protein, sweetness, and ease of prep. Combo 1 (Fruity Salad, Curd, Buns) and Combo 2 (Chicken \u0026 Cabbage Soup) look promising. However, Combo 5 (Lemony Shrimp) is a single dish and is also under consideration. Calories are the focus to keep the plan within the target.\n\n\n**Refining Breakfast Recipes**\n\nI'm now carefully curating the breakfast recipes to fit the requirements. I'm actively focusing on the \"Sweet Morning Reset,\" \"Power-Up Protein Plate,\" and the \"Zesty Shrimp \u0026 Pasta Bowl\" to create the initial active recipes. I have two more dishes to include, which will be the \"Fiber-First Kale Soup\" and \"Sweet \u0026 Savory Chicken Salad.\" I'm doing the final checks on the dish IDs to remove any repeats across the list.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Recipes**\n\nI'm deep in the final checks, ensuring no dish appears more than twice in the full breakfast selection, and that my \"active\" combos are unique. I have double checked all dishes meet the user's needs for protein, sweetness, and practicality. The subtitles are in place and the sassy, bestie tone is locked in. I'm ready to present the recipes.\n\n\n**Revising Recipe Presentation**\n\nOkay, I'm now fine-tuning the wording for each recipe, making sure they're clear, enticing, and, most importantly, in the sassy bestie tone. I've double-checked all the IDs to make sure there are no issues. I've adjusted the copy to be even more \"Jovida-esque\". I'm making a final pass, making sure the breakfast options are truly amazing!\n\n\n**Crafting Recipe Descriptions**\n\nNow, I'm perfecting the recipe presentations. I've re-written the copy to include sassy bestie tones, while making sure to include the relevant nutritional information. All dish IDs have been checked and double-checked and are ready to be used. I’m focusing on the first two recipes now.\n\n\n"},{"text":"{\n  \"recipes\": [\n    {\n      \"recipe_title\": \"The Sweet Morning Reset\",\n      \"recipe_subtitle\": \"Fruity chicken salad + tart cranberry curd + light steamed buns\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"Since your late-night hunger usually starts with a sweet craving, we’re playing offense this morning. This combo hits your dessert driver with fruit and curd while the yogurt-based chicken salad keeps your insulin from spiking, stopping the hunger cycle before it starts.\",\n      \"dishes\": [\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"93431\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Main Dish\",\n            \"High Protein\",\n            \"Sweet \u0026 Savory\",\n            \"Satiety Score\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"104682\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Side Dish\",\n            \"Sweet\",\n            \"Dessert Swap\",\n            \"Low Effort\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"104683\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Side Dish\",\n            \"Carb\",\n            \"Comfort Food\",\n            \"Brainless\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"recipe_title\": \"Power-Up Protein Plate\",\n      \"recipe_subtitle\": \"Creamy Asiago chicken + healing cabbage soup volume patch\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"Protein is your metabolic best friend for fat loss, and this Asiago chicken delivers over 30g to keep you locked in until lunch. The cabbage soup adds massive volume for very few calories, ensuring you feel physically full without the typical morning slump.\",\n      \"dishes\": [\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"93430\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Main Dish\",\n            \"High Protein\",\n            \"Stable Energy\",\n            \"Comfort Food\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"76069\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Side Dish\",\n            \"Veggie\",\n            \"Volume Patch\",\n            \"Clean / Detox\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"recipe_title\": \"Zesty Shrimp \u0026 Pasta Bowl\",\n      \"recipe_subtitle\": \"Garlic-lemon shrimp + angel hair pasta for a savory energy boost\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"If you're waking up feeling extra hungry, this high-protein shrimp bowl is a smart move. The garlic and lemon provide a savory punch that satisfies without the heavy grease, giving you a steady burn of energy for your morning steps.\",\n      \"dishes\": [\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"74173\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Complete Meal\",\n            \"High Protein\",\n            \"Savory\",\n            \"Stable Energy\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"recipe_title\": \"Fiber-First Kale Bowl\",\n      \"recipe_subtitle\": \"Kale, potatoes, and black beans for a brainless, steady start\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"Your health data shows you've been hitting your step goals lately, so let's fuel that movement with fiber. The black beans and kale in this soup provide the slow-digesting carbs your body needs to keep your energy levels flat-lined (in a good way!) all morning.\",\n      \"dishes\": [\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"92624\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Complete Meal\",\n            \"High Fiber\",\n            \"Plant-Based\",\n            \"Low Effort\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"recipe_title\": \"Tarragon Chicken Fruit Salad\",\n      \"recipe_subtitle\": \"Apples, grapes, and chicken in a creamy yogurt dressing\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"Think of this as your 'dessert for breakfast' that actually helps you lose fat. The fruit satisfies your sweet tooth, but the high-protein chicken and yogurt base prevent the sugar crash that usually leads to snacking later.\",\n      \"dishes\": [\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"93431\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Main Dish\",\n            \"High Protein\",\n            \"Sweet\",\n            \"No Cook\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"recipe_title\": \"Savory Asiago \u0026 Sweet Buns\",\n      \"recipe_subtitle\": \"Asiago chicken paired with light steamed buns and cranberry curd\",\n      \"recommendation_text\": \"This is a high-variety set that covers all your bases: savory protein, soft carbs, and a sweet finish. It’s the ultimate 'systems \u003e willpower' meal because it leaves no craving unaddressed while keeping your macros tight.\",\n      \"dishes\": [\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"93430\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Main Dish\",\n            \"High Protein\",\n            \"Savory\",\n            \"Comfort Food\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"104683\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Side Dish\",\n            \"Carb\",\n            \"Low Effort\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"dish_id\": \"104682\",\n          \"dish_labels\": [\n            \"Side Dish\",\n            \"Sweet\",\n            \"Dessert Swap\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"role":"model"}},{"role":"user","meta":{"event_type":"morning_0600","run_id":"2026022506082401KJ9PKDCEPEVV4ARJ3AAJ5JWJ","entrance":"morning_0600","history_version":1},"custom_content":{"items":[{"text":"\u003cuser_profile\u003e\n\u003cuser_basic_info\u003e\nName: codes\nGender: female\nDate of Birth: 2002-09-07\nHeight: 163.00cm\nWeight: 58.00 kg (updated on 2026-02-24)\nAge: 23\nBMI: 21.83\nbody_fat_range: 24-28%\n\n\u003c/user_basic_info\u003e\n\u003cuser_diet_info\u003e\nprimary_meal_location: Home\nmeals_per_day: 3 times\ndietary_preferences: No preference\nfood_allergies: No\nnutrition_knowledge_level: Basics (I understand the key terms. \n e.g. Calories, Protein, Carbs, Fat)\n\n\