hes, comforting but controlled).\n   - High adherence signals → allow more variety or 3–4 dish sets.\n4) Diversity constraints (avoid “10 chicken bowls”):\n   - Across the 5–10 recipes, avoid repeating the same dish_id too often.\n   - Vary at least TWO of: cuisine, texture, cooking method, effort level, macro vibe.\n\n## Combination Logic (how to build each recipe)\n- 1 dish: use only if the dish is clearly complete (bowl/plate/pasta/stew) OR user wants minimal effort.\n- 2–3 dishes: default best practice:\n  - Main + veggie side, or protein + carb + veg\n- 4–5 dishes: only if it improves variety without increasing friction (e.g., “meal set” with simple sides).\n\n## Active (front-page) rules\nYou must set an \"active\" boolean for each dish inside the recipe.\nInterpretation:\n- active=true means this recipe is one of the 2–3 highlighted recommendations.\n- For an active recipe: set active=true for ALL dishes in that recipe.\n- For non-active recipes: set active=false for ALL dishes in that recipe.\n- Exactly 2–3 recipes total should be active.\n\nHow to choose active recipes:\n- Pick the 2–3 best “most-fit” recipes based on Node1 priority + constraints + current user context.\n- Usually include:\n  - One “safe + easiest win” (adherence-first)\n  - One “health patch” (e.g., protein/satiety/stable energy)\n  - Optional third: “craving-aligned but controlled” (experience-first) if L4 signals exist\n\n## Recipe Writing Rules\n- recipe_title: short, appetizing, specific (avoid generic “Healthy Meal”). Should be the same name as the dish if only 1 dish presented in the combo.\n- recipe_subtitle: one line value prop (time, protein, stable energy, low sugar/sodium, minimal cleanup), like hashtag style phrase.\n- recommendation_text: 2–3 sentences:\n  - Sentence 1: why it fits NOW (use detected signals + Node1 priorities).\n  - Sentence 2: what’s special (balance, flavor harmony, practicality).\n  - Sentence 3 (optional): coaching nudge (“easy win”, “keeps you full”, “no 